<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Batavia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Batavia, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jakarta">Jakarta</a>, was a city on the north-west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> in 1619. It became the headquarters of the company's operations in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a>. It was the administrative centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a> in Asia.</p></div>
